-- title:
--   Determinant ℓ of Frobenius in any rank-two Hecke basis on VₚJ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \ge 1$ and a prime $p$, and assume the predicates [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8) (which asserts `HeckeInputsAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N ℓ` for every prime $\ell$) and [`ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L25) (the divisorial Hecke endomorphisms $T_\ell$ of [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115) commute pairwise). Here [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115) is the group of degree-zero divisor classes of the function field `modularFunctionFieldBar N` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, equipped with the `HeckeAlg = MvPolynomial Nat.Primes ℤ`-module structure `heckeModuleBar N` given by evaluating variables at the Hecke operators. Write $T_pJ$ for the Tate module, the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in `JZero N` with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$, and $V_p = \mathbb Q_p \otimes_{\mathbb Z_p} T_pJ$ for `RationalTateModule`; let $A =$ `rationalHeckeAlgebra p (JZero N)` be the $\mathbb Q_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Q_p}(V_p)$ generated by the image of the rational Hecke representation, and let $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ act on $V_p$ through `rationalGaloisRep`. The assertion is: for every $A$-basis $b = (b_0,b_1)$ of $V_p$ indexed by `Fin 2`, every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid Np$, every valuation subring $A'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A'$, and every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A'$ and acting on the residue field of $A'$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the coordinates $c_{ji} = (b.\mathrm{repr}(\sigma b_j))_i \in A$ satisfy $c_{00}c_{11} - c_{10}c_{01} = \ell$ in $A$.
--
--   This is the cyclotomic-determinant statement for the Galois representation on the rational Tate module of $J_0(N)$: at a Frobenius element above a prime $\ell$ of good reduction the determinant, computed over the Hecke algebra in any rank-two basis, equals $\ell$, which is the Weil-pairing half of the Eichler–Shimura description of $\mathrm{Frob}_\ell$ with characteristic polynomial $X^2 - T_\ell X + \ell$. It feeds [`ModularCurve.rationalRankTwoCyclotomic_family`](thm.html#ModularCurve.rationalRankTwoCyclotomic_family), where existence of such a basis together with this determinant formula is packaged for use in the modularity argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_frobenius_coordDet_eq_of_basis_rationalTateModule_jZero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JZeroTateModule
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeModule
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.frobenius_coordDet_eq_of_basis_rationalTateModule_jZero
    (N p : ℕ) [NeZero N] [Fact p.Prime]
    (hin : ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N) (hcomm : ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N) :
    letI := ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar N
    ∀ (b : Module.Basis (Fin 2) (ModularCurve.rationalHeckeAlgebra p (ModularCurve.JZero N))
        (ModularCurve.RationalTateModule p (ModularCurve.JZero N)))
      (ℓ : ℕ), ℓ.Prime → ¬ ℓ ∣ N * p →
      ∀ A' : ValuationSubring (AlgebraicClosure ℚ), A'.LiesOverPrime ℓ →
        ∀ σ : AlgebraicClosure ℚ ≃ₐ[ℚ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ, A'.IsFrobeniusAt σ ℓ →
          (b.repr (ModularCurve.rationalGaloisRep p (ModularCurve.JZero N)
                (AlgebraicClosure ℚ ≃ₐ[ℚ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ) σ (b 0))) 0
              * (b.repr (ModularCurve.rationalGaloisRep p (ModularCurve.JZero N)
                (AlgebraicClosure ℚ ≃ₐ[ℚ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ) σ (b 1))) 1
            - (b.repr (ModularCurve.rationalGaloisRep p (ModularCurve.JZero N)
                (AlgebraicClosure ℚ ≃ₐ[ℚ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ) σ (b 1))) 0
              * (b.repr (ModularCurve.rationalGaloisRep p (ModularCurve.JZero N)
                (AlgebraicClosure ℚ ≃ₐ[ℚ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ) σ (b 0))) 1
            = (ℓ : ModularCurve.rationalHeckeAlgebra p (ModularCurve.JZero N)) := by sorry
